Subject: [PATCH 3/5] platform/x86: int3472: Add GPIO type 0x08 (DVDD) and 0x10
 (DOVDD) support

Add proper handling for GPIO types seen on Microsoft Surface Pro 10
cameras that were previously unknown to the driver:

- GPIO type 0x08: DVDD secondary digital core voltage, mapped to
  'dvdd2' consumer ID via new INT3472_GPIO_TYPE_DVDD constant
- GPIO type 0x10: DOVDD digital I/O voltage, already handled by
  existing INT3472_GPIO_TYPE_DOVDD but previously not reached due
  to missing case in switch statement

Without this fix, int3472-discrete logs 'GPIO type 0x08 unknown'
and the sensor may not receive correct power sequencing.

Replaces the Surface Pro 9 workaround which used raw magic numbers
(0x08, 0x10) with proper named constants.

Patchset: cameras
