From c09b1a55bdfc1b3b3943ef93d7f6c4428a97e8d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.J. Mulder" <djmulder@example.com>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 15:58:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] platform/x86: int3472: Mark clock critical and regulators
 always-on for SP10

On Microsoft Surface Pro 10, the INT3472 clock and regulators must
remain active across probe sequences to avoid camera sensor failures:

- Add CLK_IS_CRITICAL flag to prevent the clock framework from
  disabling the sensor clock during probe/reprobe cycles
- Set boot_on and always_on constraints on regulators to ensure
  power rails are maintained during device_reprobe()

Without these changes, the OV13858 rear camera fails to probe when
device_reprobe() is called after ipu-bridge attaches the fwnode,
as the clock and power rails are disabled between probe attempts.

Patchset: cameras
