From 5f303220052fe7290be7d93a43cfdaa3be874892 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.J. Mulder" <djmulder@example.com>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 15:58:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] media: i2c: ov13858: Add reset GPIO handling for Surface
 Pro 10

The OV13858 rear camera on Microsoft Surface Pro 10 requires explicit
reset GPIO toggling during probe to bring the sensor out of hardware
reset before register access is attempted.

- Add reset GPIO acquisition via devm_gpiod_get_optional()
- Toggle reset high for 20ms then low with 50ms stabilisation delay
- Enable clock before reset sequence as required by sensor datasheet
- Add linux/gpio/consumer.h and linux/delay.h includes

Without this fix the sensor remains in reset and all I2C register
reads return 0xFF, causing probe to fail with -EIO on chip ID check.

Patchset: cameras
